1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,120
Another thing with the buses I learned the hard way that you have to flag down the bus if you want it to stop for you.
关于公交，我吃了亏才学到：如果想让公交停车，得挥手示意。

2
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:12,780
So even though I was kind of standing at the side of the bus stop.
当时我就站在公交站旁边。

3
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:17,940
And there was only one bus that stopped at the stop I was at the guy just kept driving.
虽然我所在的站只有那一路公交，但司机还是直接开走了。

4
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:25,380
So yeah if you want to catch the bus you have to stand outside and flag them down lesson learned.
所以想乘车，就站出来挥手示意。我记住这个教训了。

5
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:36,120
Something that I didn't like so much that I thought was strange especially because of all of the tech companies and multinational corporations that are based in dublin.
有件让我不太喜欢、也觉得奇怪的事，尤其考虑到都柏林有那么多科技公司和跨国企业。

6
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:39,960
Is how slow the internet is.
那就是我感觉网络很慢。

7
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:51,180
The wi fi is really slow at hotels at my airbnb and also the 5 g connection on my phone with my local sim card was also pretty slow.
酒店和 Airbnb 的无线网络很慢，我用当地 SIM 卡时，手机5G连接也挺慢。

8
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:57,600
So in some countries you can get 50 or 100 megabit downloads per second on your phone.
在某些国家，手机每秒可以下载五十或一百兆比特。

9
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:06,120
And here it was like 10 to 15 to 20 whereas my wi fi has been like one to five megabits per second.
而我在这里大约只有十、十五到二十；无线网络大概每秒一到五兆比特。

10
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:15,000
So I've heard that that is pretty common throughout dublin and possibly the rest of the country but that's something that really surprised me.
我听说都柏林、可能全国很多地方都常有这种情况，但它还是让我很意外。

11
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:24,470
Something else I wasn't expecting is to hear that the population still hasn't recovered from the famine of the 1840 s.
另一个我没想到的听闻，是人口仍未从十九世纪四十年代饥荒的影响中恢复。

12
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:31,139
Over 1 million people are estimated to have died during that time and many immigrated as well.
作者说，据估计那段时期有超过一百万人死亡，也有很多人迁移；immigrated 的原词待核。

13
00:01:31,139 --> 00:01:39,540
And so the country is still trying to rebuild its population from hundreds of years ago so that was quite shocking.
她说，这个国家仍在从几百年前的人口变化中恢复，这让她相当震惊。

14
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:49,370
I also didn't expect to find a japanese zen garden in an irish village but here we are.
我也没想到会在爱尔兰村庄里找到日式禅意花园，但我们现在就在这里。

15
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:56,950
Something that really confused me is that there don't seem to be any electrical plugs in any of the bathrooms.
有件事让我困惑：浴室里似乎都没有电源插座。

16
00:01:56,960 --> 00:02:06,480
Now at first I thought it was just my hotel but it was also at my airbnb and I noticed other people talking about it.
起初我以为只有自己的酒店这样，但 Airbnb 也是，我还注意到别人也在讨论。

17
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:10,260
So yeah apparently there's no plugs in the bathroom.
所以看起来浴室里没有插座。

18
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:19,199
So when you go to look for your hair dryer look in the kitchen or in a drawer in the desk or something like that.
找吹风机时，去厨房、书桌抽屉等地方找找。

19
00:02:19,199 --> 00:02:22,859
And you may have to blow dry your hair in the living room.
而且你可能得在客厅里吹头发。

20
00:02:22,859 --> 00:02:29,940
On the plus side though just like in the uk you can actually turn off the individual electrical outlets.
不过好的一面是，像英国一样，你实际上可以单独关闭各个电源插座。

21
00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:33,479
So I think that's really cool and I wish we had that in the us as well.
我觉得这很棒，也希望美国有这样的设计。

22
00:02:33,479 --> 00:02:38,220
I remember when I was in college my roommate used to unplug all of the appliances.
记得大学时，我的室友会把所有电器插头拔掉。

23
00:02:38,220 --> 00:02:46,430
So we could save money on our electrical bill and yeah if we just had plugs that you could turn on and off we wouldn't have to do that.
那样可以省电费。如果有能直接开关的插座，我们就不用拔插头了。

24
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:54,409
Something that I thought was really cool is that all of the signage and the road signs are in english as well as irish.
我还觉得很棒的是，所有标识和路牌都有英语和爱尔兰语。

25
00:02:54,419 --> 00:03:01,560
And even though I knew that irish was an official language here I didn't expect to see all of the signs in irish.
虽然我知道爱尔兰语是这里的官方语言，我还是没想到所有标牌上都会看到它。

26
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:05,460
So I think that that's really cool and it looks like quite a difficult language to learn.
我觉得这很棒，而且它看上去是门挺难学的语言。

27
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:12,469
But something else that really surprised me is that it could be quite normal for people to be late around here.
另一件让我意外的事，是在她听来的描述中，人们在这里迟到可能相当平常。

28
00:03:12,479 --> 00:03:16,740
And that's not something that's very customary throughout Europe.
这不是她觉得欧洲其他地方普遍惯有的做法。

29
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:26,269
So I was pretty surprised to hear that yeah people could be 15 minutes late an hour late and it's really no big deal.
所以听说有人会迟到十五分钟、一小时，而且不算大事，我挺吃惊。

30
00:03:26,279 --> 00:03:36,360
But also things are open quite late so I notice people out having dinner really late like 10 p m 11 p m clubs are open till 3 a m.
此外，营业时间也很晚。我看到有人晚上十点、十一点吃饭，俱乐部营业到凌晨三点。

31
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:46,260
And then there's also people out and about like just walking around on the streets in the middle of the night having kebabs and things at four or five in the morning.
还有人半夜在街上活动，凌晨四五点吃烤肉之类的食物。

32
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:53,700
So I was surprised at how lively the nightlife was and how late people were out and about.
夜生活这么热闹、大家这么晚还在外面，让我很惊讶。

33
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:58,440
And the towns outside of dublin have quite interesting names.
都柏林周边的城镇，名字也相当有趣。
